<p><strong>2. The $50,000 Per Home Cap</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Each eligible household is capped at $50,000 for disaster-related repairs</li>
<li>This is per disaster, per home (if another disaster hits, new cap applies)</li>
<li>Funds must be spent on eligible repairs only</li>
<li>The cap applies to total cost across all funding sources</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>3. How We Track Funding Per Case</strong></p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Approved Amount</strong>: What we\'ve committed to spend</li>
<li><strong>Incurred Costs</strong>: What we\'ve actually spent (invoices, materials, labor)</li>
<li><strong>Reimbursed Amount</strong>: What has been paid out</li>
<li><strong>Remaining Balance</strong>: What\'s left to spend</li>
<li><strong>On Hold</strong>: Money set aside for pending items</li>
</ul>
